    "title": "DTG-associated weight gain and pre-diabetes risk",
    "message": "Guidelines state DTG-based regimens have been associated with weight gain and that antiretroviral drugs are a major cause of diabetes in PLHIV. DTG should not be used in patients who develop diabetes. This patient gained 17kg and her BMI rose from 25.6 to 32.4 over 18 months on TLD. She now has impaired fasting glucose (118 mg/dL), HbA1c 6.1%, acanthosis nigricans, and a family history of Type 2 diabetes. Evidence for drug attribution: the temporal relationship between DTG initiation and rapid weight gain is strong, and DTG is a recognised cause. Evidence against: baseline BMI was already 25.6 and family history confers independent diabetes risk. Metabolically neutral ARVs (ABC, TDF, 3TC) are recommended for patients at risk of DM.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Assess for diabetes using DM screening tool. Consider substituting DTG with a metabolically neutral ARV. Counsel on weight loss, diet, and exercise. Monitor fasting glucose and HbA1c regularly.",
