    "title": "Elevated BP and dyslipidaemia require management plan",
    "message": "Guidelines state the goal of treatment is blood pressure below 140/90 mmHg and that uncontrolled hypertension and blood sugar may cause complications including heart attack, stroke, and chronic kidney disease. This patient's BP is 138/88 mmHg, up from a baseline of 118/74, borderline to the target. She also has a significantly atherogenic lipid profile (LDL 148, HDL 38, triglycerides 212). Her compounding risks — obesity, pre-diabetes, dyslipidaemia, and rising BP — substantially increase cardiovascular risk. No assessment or plan was documented for these abnormalities.",
